# IAM safety

Apply least privilege. Do not add `*` actions, `*` resources, or administrator
policies unless the repository already uses that pattern with explicit guardrails.

Prefer IAM roles, instance profiles, and IRSA over long-lived access keys. Never
hardcode access keys, secret ARNs, or session tokens in source or IaC.

When editing policies or trust relationships, verify principals, conditions, and
external IDs match existing modules. Do not broaden trust to `*` principals.

Review policy diffs for new `iam:PassRole`, `sts:AssumeRole`, or cross-account
access before apply.
